# A founding-file rule entry ('#### <slug>') with no text is a hard error
# (exit 2), not a silently-dropped rule: rule input is validated, never
# silently swallowed. So is a present-but-empty '## Rules' section. The
# message names the offending rule/section. Nothing is seeded.

env CONSTITUTION_TODAY=2026-07-02

# --- '#### <slug>' with no text beneath it ---
exitcode 2 constitution init --founding-file principles.md
stderr 'rule "testing/no-text" has no text'
! exists constitution/adr/ADR-0001-tests-are-mandatory.md

# --- '## Rules' present but empty ---
exitcode 2 constitution init --founding-file empty-rules.md
stderr 'the "## Rules" section is present but empty'
! exists constitution/adr/ADR-0001-tests-are-mandatory.md

-- principles.md --
## Tests are mandatory

Every change ships with tests.

## Rules

### testing

#### no-text

-- empty-rules.md --
## Tests are mandatory

Every change ships with tests.

## Rules
